---
description: API clients and specs use env-based URLs and body assertions
globs: src/api/**/*.ts,tests/api/**/*.ts
alwaysApply: false
---

# API tests

- Call `AuthApi` or a future client. Do not `request.post` host URLs from specs.
- Build paths from `API_BASE_URL` via `env.ts`. Never hardcode environments.
- Assert HTTP status and response body shape.

```typescript
// BAD
await request.post('https://prod.example.com/api/v1/auth/login/');

// GOOD
const response = await authApi.login(brandEmail, brandPassword);
expect(response.ok()).toBeTruthy();
expect((await response.json()).tokens?.access_token).toBeTruthy();
```
